Milestone: Peer feedback collection and an owner-reviewed planned-work document.
Dependencies: Existing public BowserBOY deployment and actual reviewer responses.
Purpose: Collect evidence-grounded feedback, preserve every recommendation's
disposition, and plan improvements without implementing unapproved changes.

Tasks:
- [x] Publish a new mandatory room-wide review thread with the live URL,
  isolated local setup, source guide, response format and evidence boundaries.
- [x] Save the consultation, due date, recipient coverage and approval gate
  in owned continuity; register a session-scoped five-day review prompt.
- [ ] On or after 2026-11-15 21:15 Asia/Kolkata, reconcile actual replies.
- [ ] Create numbered eight-field TODOs for distinct recommendations; preserve
  attribution, evidence, duplicates, conflicts and explicit dispositions.
- [ ] Continue bounded reviews until feedback is quiet; report missing members
  and access blockers instead of treating silence as approval.
- [ ] Deliver the consolidated planned-work document for the owner's decision.

Acceptance criteria:
Read existing replies first: two reviewers must not submit the same feedback.
Require distinct observations/evidence, not copied or reworded recommendations;
link prior findings and add a genuinely different contribution. Never fabricate
issues or testing merely to make feedback unique.
The review distinguishes the public revision from uncommitted local features.
Every indexed member is requested to provide an individual substantive review,
or explicitly report access/tool limitations and label source-only conclusions.
The consultation cannot fabricate peer activity or wake dormant agents.
No recommendation is lost merely because issue/Project synchronization agrees.
Recommendation TODOs remain NOT_STARTED and explicitly awaiting owner approval.
The final plan explains proposed changes, rationale, acceptance, dependencies,
risks, estimated scope and source feedback; uncertain claims stay unverified.
The owner's explicit green signal is required before implementation.
No application changes, commit, push or deployment are authorized by this task.

